1️⃣ PROFILE PHOTO (don’t skip this)
✅ What to do

Clear headshot
Plain background (white/grey)
Natural light
Professional but not stiff

You don’t need a studio photo. Phone camera is fine.
✅ Why it matters
Profiles with photos get ~10x more views than without.

2️⃣ HEADLINE (MOST IMPORTANT SECTION)
Recruiters search by headline keywords.
If this is wrong, nothing else matters.
❌ Don’t use

“Software Engineer at Capgemini”
“Aspiring AI Engineer”
“Python Developer | Learning AI”

These kill seniority.

✅ USE THIS HEADLINE (copy‑paste)
Option A (recommended):
AI Backend Engineer | GenAI (OCR + LLM Pipelines) | FastAPI, Python | Capgemini

Option B (slightly more global):
AI Backend Engineer | Production GenAI Systems | OCR, LLMs, FastAPI | Capgemini

✅ Why this works

Clear role identity ✅
“AI Backend Engineer” appears FIRST ✅
Keywords recruiters actually search ✅
No exaggeration ✅

✅ Use Option A if you want clarity.
✅ Use Option B if you want broader global appeal.

