4️⃣ ABOUT SECTION (THIS IS NOT YOUR RESUME)
This is where most people go wrong.
❌ Don’t

Copy resume bullets
Write 10 paragraphs
Talk about “learning journey”

✅ DO THIS INSTEAD
Use 6–8 strong lines.
✅ COPY‑PASTE ABOUT SECTION
AI Backend Engineer working on production Generative AI systems within enterprise environments.

I specialize in building FastAPI-based backend services that integrate OCR and LLM pipelines, with a strong focus on AI reliability, confidence scoring, and human-in-the-loop validation.

At Capgemini, I contribute to medical-domain AI applications preparing for international deployment, collaborating closely with senior backend engineers and solving real production challenges.

I am interested in AI backend roles where production quality, system design, and real-world impact matter more than demos.

✅ Why this is strong

You sound like a practitioner, not a learner
Clear backend + AI focus
Enterprise + production credibility
Works for Mumbai and abroad


5️⃣ EXPERIENCE SECTION (SYNC WITH RESUME)
✅ Job title (important)
Change your title to:
Software Engineer – AI Backend

✅ This is accurate
✅ This helps recruiters classify you correctly

✅ Description (5–6 bullets max)
Use shorter versions of your resume bullets.
COPY‑PASTE (edit dates only):
• Working as a backend engineer on production medical-domain applications integrating OCR outputs with LLM pipelines using FastAPI.
• Implementing API logic for input validation, response normalization, error handling, and AI reliability.
• Integrating Tesseract OCR with LLM workflows to process and interpret medical text data.
• Designing human-in-the-loop validation using confidence scoring for low-reliability AI outputs.
• Collaborating with senior backend engineers on code reviews, design discussions, and production issue resolution.
• Presenting AI system architecture and impact to senior leadership stakeholders.

✅ Why this works

Clear AI backend focus
Not tool dumping
Matches resume → builds trust


